    {
      "id": "evidence-000-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Measured 2026-08-15: 1024 subsets swept, 640 containing a reported key, 384 issued a counterexample relation and 384 of those checked. 3520 removal tests, ALL DECIDED -- attribute closure is a total function on a finite lattice, so no budget can make one `unknown`, and the minimality claim is therefore ABSOLUTE in the sense of ADR-0455 rather than budget-relative. The sweep also fails if a subset containing a reported key turns out not to be a superkey, or if a subset containing none turns out to be one, which is what makes the list COMPLETE rather than merely correct. Each reported key additionally carries a replayed Armstrong derivation of key -> R.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "d637d83f77dbfa43c98eee4ab0ad78d235099006",
