    {
      "id": "evidence-001-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Five of the seven dependencies violate BCNF; the same five violate 3NF because each has a non-prime attribute on the right. The prime attributes -- line_uuid, order_id, line_no -- come from the exhaustive sweep above, so the 3NF verdict inherits its completeness. The BCNF verdict examines only the dependencies IN F, which is sufficient by an argument recorded in the module documentation and carried in the axiom footprint as the one assumption here that is a theorem rather than a measurement.",
